#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Drive prwatch's change detection with made-up data and check what it says.

The events worth having are the rare ones, and the rare ones are the ones a
live pull request will not produce on demand: a cancelled run, a check that
goes back to pending, a branch that starts conflicting, a commit with no CI
at all. This feeds those situations to the same methods the watcher uses and
compares the lines that come out.

Run it with no arguments. It touches no network and no repository.
"""

